p to make sure that she is working on that.</p><p>Megan Gordon: She said she was going to start them today. She was waiting on the workflow.</p><p>Bob Duncan: That&#x27;s fine. So that will get done. Are you wanting me to?</p><p>Megan Gordon: Share the spreadsheet.</p><p>Bob Duncan: If you can, just so we can have a little look and see roughly what business pipeline is sitting there. I&#x27;ll give us a bit of an idea.</p><p>Speaker 5: How are you doing? The callbacks are filtered, Stephen. Here you go.</p><p>Bob Duncan: So We are which one? One next one here&#x27;s our.</p><p>Megan Gordon: I&#x27;m assuming it&#x27;ll be here.</p><p>Bob Duncan: That&#x27;s fine, and then it&#x27;ll also be the ones for the following month as well.</p><p>Megan Gordon: I think so. This sort of last batch here.</p><p>Bob Duncan: Do we need to update the spreadsheet then? I know that does it.</p><p>Megan Gordon: So I don&#x27;t know as in you need to drop an action of, probably right? That&#x27;s fine. I&#x27;ll take that as an action point.</p><p>Bob Duncan: I bring up all the leads. That&#x27;s what I&#x27;m trying to do. End of that one.</p><p>Speaker 5: But at this, whoever brought that on at this stage, Margaret back again, said the same thing as a step</p><p>Bob Duncan: We need to do it.</p><p>Speaker 5: She feels the property requires a bit of work and doesn&#x27;t see the value added to her home. It&#x27;s not going to work. She&#x27;s had this problem.</p><p>Holly newton: I&#x27;ll see if I can fix my mic. Is that better?</p><p>Bob Duncan: That&#x27;s a hundred times better.</p><p>Holly newton: That&#x27;s noise suppression off, so I&#x27;ll just do that from now on.</p><p>Bob Duncan: Reports here we go, this is what I was looking for</p><p>Bob Duncan: And we want it to be by oh my gosh, this is wrecking my head. Roland&#x27;s.</p><p>Speaker 6: There we go. It might be easier just to export that and then.</p><p>Speaker 6: I&#x27;m going to initiate a. We need to have a little 