d your time making sure you&#x27;re updating this every single day would be my advice to you, because if you don&#x27;t, you&#x27;ll end up in a position where some people have got 30 or 40, and it becomes a bit of a mammoth task. It&#x27;s exactly what you were doing in Midas, and I know we&#x27;re kind of using both at the moment, which is a bit crap. But as we continue to keep using Platform, we will just be in Platform. And everybody that we have in Midas effectively will just be in Platform at some point in the near future if it&#x27;s not too long until that happens. And on the full remortgage journey, that&#x27;s now going to be in Platform. So they&#x27;ll no longer be in Midas or they won&#x27;t start on Midas; they&#x27;re actually going to start on Platform.</p><p>Bob Duncan: All the documents transfer it all and then use the AI etc. How are you getting on with using AI?</p><p>Roland Brownlee: I used it on the bank statements for that limited company, and it was quite freaky. It really is. As well, I saw Leeds sent something out saying they&#x27;re going to start using open banking in the background. Yes, I am using it.</p><p>Bob Duncan: Definitely use it where you can. I would definitely say it speeds the case up. And certainly, if you&#x27;ve got the payslips element and you&#x27;ve got the bank statements, and that is doing the hard work for you, it is going to save you a minimum of an hour, I would think, if you&#x27;re using it to do all that for the bank statements and payslips. You&#x27;ve got three payslips, two months worth of bank statements. That&#x27;s done for you just like that. Amazing. So definitely 100% worthwhile doing. So if you&#x27;re not doing it, I would absolutely encourage you to actually start doing it. The same with depths and platform.</p><p>Roland Brownlee: I&#x27;ve used it once. I haven&#x27;t used it since.</p><p>Bob Duncan: Why is that?</p><p>Roland Brownlee: I don&#x27;t know. Maybe because my full fact find wasn&#x27;t completed. I don&#x27;t think you can do it so I take enough information for a depth. But that&#x27;s not the full fact find, if you know what I mean. The full fact find needs to be completed before you can do it, so that would probably be why. But I have done it and I have got a pass and a certificate out of it before, so I need to learn to fill the full fact find out.</p><p>Bob Duncan: The full fact find is very much like what you&#x27;ll probably find you&#x27;re missing is the mortgage numbers. What&#x27;s the mortgage? What&#x27;s the deposit? How much do you want to borrow? What&#x27;s mortgage term? Is it fixed or is it a tracker? Are they a first time buyer? Are they a home mover? Have you completed the budget planner? It will be really, really basic things. Have you got a case that you&#x27;ve done recently that you dealt elsewhere, but you didn&#x27;t deal with them platform? So any of these that you&#x27;ve got.</p><p>Roland Brownlee: No agent movies. No John Colin Wilkie. The one this morning. Who was that? Let me get him out.</p><p>Bob Duncan: I&#x27;ll look for them or her.</p><p>Speaker 6: Or them</p><p>Speaker 7: Or they.</p><p>Roland Brownlee: It was. Surname is Chowdhary, so not Chowdhury. Chowdhary C H O W D H A R Y. Say that.</p><p>Bob Duncan: Again C H.</p><p>Roland Brownlee: O W D H A R Y Why are they not on platform? It should be C H O W D H E R Y this one here.</p><p>Bob Duncan: So let&#x27;s go. And we&#x27;ll do a fact check. And then if we do advisor summary, we&#x27;ve not ticked the credit history button. We&#x27;ve not put in the purchase price. We&#x27;ve not put in the term. We&#x27;ve not said if it&#x27;s loan or cost effective. We&#x27;ve not put in the property type. Not the own title type, so it must be a message. We&#x27;re not going to put anything in no build. Not the mortgage type.</p><p>Roland Brownlee: Is it only that you need to fill in to do it? I thought it was every single box.</p><p>Bob Duncan: So everything, if you look at every single box, you will find that there is a lot that says optional.</p><p>Roland Brownlee: So.</p><p>Bob Duncan: You&#x27;ve got optional main residence. What&#x27;s purchase price of the property? We&#x27;ll just say it&#x27;s hundred and fifty thousand. How much can we afford? Say fifteen hundred. See its overall costs. What&#x27;s the mortgage term you&#x27;re thinking of? Thirty. Thirty years flat. Not a self build. It&#x27;s going to be a freehold in Scotland, and it&#x27;s not going to be new build and you&#x27;re buying in Scotland and I&#x27;m assuming you&#x27;re getting taxed two years. There&#x27;s five years just two to begin with two and I&#x27;m assuming you want to do this team.</p><p>Bob Duncan: So there we go. Done. Now you&#x27;re</p><p>Roland Brownlee: It&#x27;s so where did you get those red boxes? Go into advisor summary.</p><p>Bob Duncan: Actually, just literally click on advisor summary that&#x27;ll tell you what you&#x27;re missing. As you can see there, we just whipped through that and not even a minute. And you know, a possession where we can lock down the fact find. And if you want to request a decision on principle and then you&#x27;ll come back and get your result. You would be able to add your mortgage passport. So you got this lead yet already?</p><p>Roland Brownlee: I&#x27;m struggling. I&#x27;ve got an eighty five percent from Halifax and nothing, so I&#x27;ve requested a report. Let&#x27;s see what&#x27;s behind it. So can I then unlock that if detail changes?</p><p>Bob Duncan: Absolutely can. You can just unlock it purely for you. Then you can go and edit some of the information. You could add in here, you could check the requirements. Then all you do is just go back to the very end, and it asks you again, are you happy to confirm? Don&#x27;t tick the top one because that&#x27;s ticking that they&#x27;re a mortgage prisoner. We want it to be a bit bolder. And then by hitting submit, it locks it down and then you&#x27;re in