dd hundred eleven, and then April was a hundred and two. And then you&#x27;ve got it broken down by products or purchases.</p><p>Bob Duncan: I&#x27;m not one with the new WhatsApp on it. Just like to get to quite up along because in January, you&#x27;re averaging cover sixty k for a purchase. In March it was one hundred and fifty eighty three for a remortgage. So you&#x27;re definitely not at the low end. Unless you&#x27;re keying the incoming correct on the system.</p><p>Roland Brownlee: No</p><p>Bob Duncan: That&#x27;s what we&#x27;re not doing now.</p><p>Bob Duncan: It would definitely sit in that kind of high end market, and that is the kind of people we should be attracting. If I ask you, why would you want to speak to them? What would your answer be?</p><p>Roland Brownlee: I can convert them. What else? Why do I want to speak to it? Because they need more protection. Protection means more income at the end of the day, more income.</p><p>Bob Duncan: You think they&#x27;re likely to want advice. Why do you think that is?</p><p>Roland Brownlee: Because they&#x27;re busy with their jobs and they can&#x27;t be bothered with the hassle. They respect your advice. Do you think they pay a fee?</p><p>Bob Duncan: They usually do. I get annoyed at people earning eighty grand who don&#x27;t pay a fee, and then people at twenty five do. Don&#x27;t think that&#x27;s fair. Completely agree with you.</p><p>Roland Brownlee: So yes, they should and they normally do.</p><p>Bob Duncan: So my point there is that this is the average person that you&#x27;re dealing with. If we then just bring in the rest of the business as a whole into this, I am just looking at the first half of the year here, you can see that it does change. I don&#x27;t know what happened there where we&#x27;ve got buy to let somebody&#x27;s put five hundred and eighty eight thousand. I think that is an absolute blunder.</p><p>Roland Brownlee: Of income.</p><p>Bob Duncan: That is not right. I feel like that&#x27;s